      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that if someone creates a child class of FakeSecureHardwareProvisioningProxy, call it FakeChild, and it overrides shutdown() with its own implementation, but code destructs the instance via a FakeSecureHardwareProvisioningProxy pointer, then we won\u0027t invoke FakeChild::shutdown() here, because we don\u0027t use the dynamic/virtual binding in destructors (or constructors).\n\nThis might not be of any concern.  If we\u0027re worried, we could declare shutdown() \u0027final\u0027 in the header for this class, to prevent this situation.",
      "revId": "1eb12b29728adcbbe5b8694f671c67b8a624fe4a",
