      "message": "I definitely see in the code where, if initialize() returns with success, then \"id_\" and \"authChallenge_\" will be initialized.\n\nHowever, before initialize() is called, and in some of the error cases that initialize() returns, these two variables will be uninitialized memory.  Are we worried about calls into getSessionId() and/or getAuthChallenge(...) in those situations?\n\nI don\u0027t know the context of this code, but this seems to deal with some level of authentication.  I wonder if it might be worth initializing these two fields to known values, either 0 or UINT64_C(-1), in the constructor so we don\u0027t need to worry about any possible uninitialized usage.",
